---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const lastUpdated = '21 August 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | PACTSOL"
  description="Privacy Policy explaining how PACTSOL handles personal and business contact information in connection with its website and managed B2B sourcing activities."
>
  <section class="legal-page">
    <div class="site-container legal-page__container">

      <header class="legal-page__header">
        <p class="legal-page__eyebrow">
          Legal
        </p>

        <h1>
          Privacy Policy
        </h1>

        <p class="legal-page__updated">
          Last updated: {lastUpdated}
        </p>

        <p class="legal-page__intro">
          This Privacy Policy explains how PACTSOL may collect, use, share,
          retain, and otherwise handle personal information in connection
          with the PACTSOL website, sourcing enquiries, supplier
          communications, and related business interactions.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="legal-page__notice">
        <strong>In simple terms:</strong>&nbsp;PACTSOL primarily needs business contact and sourcing information to
        understand enquiries, communicate with customers and suppliers, and
        coordinate relevant sourcing activity. Please do not provide
        unnecessary personal, confidential, or sensitive information.
      </div>

      <div class="legal-page__content">

        <section>
          <h2>1. About This Policy</h2>

          <p>
            This Privacy Policy applies to personal information handled by
            PACTSOL through its website, email, telephone communications,
            sourcing enquiries, supplier capability submissions, and related
            business activities.
          </p>

          <p>
            PACTSOL operates primarily in a business-to-business context.
            Nevertheless, business communications may contain personal
            information relating to individual employees, proprietors,
            representatives, customers, suppliers, or other business
            contacts.
          </p>

          <p>
            This Policy should be read together with PACTSOL's Terms &
            Conditions and any transaction-specific terms that may apply to
            a particular business engagement.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>2. Information PACTSOL May Collect</h2>

          <p>
            Depending on how you interact with PACTSOL, information collected
            or received may include:
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>your name;</li>
            <li>business or organisation name;</li>
            <li>job title or business role;</li>
            <li>business email address;</li>
            <li>telephone or mobile number;</li>
            <li>business address or delivery location;</li>
            <li>
              product descriptions, specifications, quantities, delivery
              requirements, timelines, and other sourcing information;
            </li>
            <li>
              supplier product categories, capabilities, commercial
              information, certifications, or business credentials;
            </li>
            <li>
              quotations, commercial correspondence, clarification messages,
              and other communications exchanged with PACTSOL;
            </li>
            <li>
              information reasonably necessary for invoicing, accounting,
              payment administration, tax compliance, or transaction records,
              where applicable; and
            </li>
            <li>
              limited technical information generated when the website is
              accessed, where such information is made available through
              hosting, security, server, or similar technical infrastructure.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>3. Information PACTSOL Does Not Normally Need</h2>

          <p>
            PACTSOL's ordinary sourcing process does not require users to
            provide passwords, banking passwords, card PINs, authentication
            codes, private account credentials, medical records, or other
            highly sensitive personal information unrelated to a legitimate
            business transaction.
          </p>

          <p>
            Please do not send such information unless PACTSOL has
            specifically requested information for a lawful and necessary
            purpose and an appropriate method of communication has been
            identified.
          </p>

          <p>
            Users should also avoid providing personal information about
            another person unless they are authorised to do so.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>4. How Information Is Collected</h2>

          <p>
            PACTSOL may receive information when you:
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>contact PACTSOL by email or telephone;</li>
            <li>submit or discuss a sourcing requirement;</li>
            <li>request a quotation or sourcing assistance;</li>
            <li>share supplier capabilities or product information;</li>
            <li>respond to a PACTSOL sourcing or commercial communication;</li>
            <li>exchange quotations or transaction-related documents;</li>
            <li>visit or interact with the PACTSOL website; or</li>
            <li>
              otherwise provide information during a legitimate business
              interaction.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <p>
            PACTSOL may also receive business contact or supplier information
            from publicly available business sources, referrals, commercial
            directories, manufacturers, distributors, suppliers, customers,
            or other legitimate business contacts where such use is
            appropriate and lawful.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>5. Why PACTSOL Uses Information</h2>

          <p>
            PACTSOL may use relevant information for purposes including:
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>reviewing and responding to sourcing enquiries;</li>
            <li>understanding product and commercial requirements;</li>
            <li>requesting necessary clarification;</li>
            <li>identifying or approaching potentially relevant suppliers;</li>
            <li>coordinating quotations and commercial information;</li>
            <li>
              communicating with customers, manufacturers, distributors,
              suppliers, and other relevant business parties;
            </li>
            <li>administering supplier capability information;</li>
            <li>facilitating legitimate business discussions;</li>
            <li>
              preparing or maintaining quotations, invoices, transaction
              records, and related business documentation where applicable;
            </li>
            <li>maintaining reasonable internal business records;</li>
            <li>
              detecting, preventing, or responding to fraud, misuse, unlawful
              activity, security incidents, or other business risks;
            </li>
            <li>complying with applicable legal or regulatory obligations;</li>
            <li>establishing, exercising, or defending legal rights; and</li>
            <li>
              improving PACTSOL's sourcing processes, website, and business
              operations.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <p>
            PACTSOL will not intentionally use personal information for a
            materially unrelated purpose merely because that information
            happens to be available.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>6. Sharing Information for Sourcing Purposes</h2>

          <p>
            A managed sourcing service requires relevant information to be
            communicated between appropriate commercial parties.
          </p>

          <p>
            Where reasonably necessary to evaluate or progress a sourcing
            requirement, PACTSOL may share relevant product, quantity,
            specification, delivery, commercial, or business contact
            information with manufacturers, distributors, suppliers, or
            other parties involved in assessing the requirement.
          </p>

          <p>
            PACTSOL will seek to limit such sharing to information reasonably
            relevant to the sourcing or commercial purpose. However, users
            should understand that information included in a sourcing brief
            may need to be communicated to potential supply sources in order
            to obtain meaningful commercial responses.
          </p>

          <p>
            Customers should therefore avoid including confidential
            information in an initial enquiry unless that information is
            genuinely necessary.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>7. Service Providers and Business Support</h2>

          <p>
            PACTSOL may use third-party service providers to support website
            hosting, email delivery, communications, cybersecurity,
            anti-spam protection, document handling, accounting, analytics,
            professional advice, or other legitimate business functions.
          </p>

          <p>
            Where such providers process information on PACTSOL's behalf,
            PACTSOL may provide information reasonably necessary for the
            relevant service.
          </p>

          <p>
            The specific providers used by PACTSOL may change as its
            technology and business operations develop. PACTSOL does not
            intend to provide service providers with unrelated personal
            information merely because they supply a service.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>8. Other Circumstances in Which Information May Be Shared</h2>

          <p>
            PACTSOL may disclose relevant information where reasonably
            necessary:
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>to comply with applicable law or a lawful authority;</li>
            <li>
              to respond to a valid court order, regulatory request, or legal
              process;
            </li>
            <li>
              to investigate suspected fraud, unlawful conduct, security
              incidents, or misuse;
            </li>
            <li>
              to protect the lawful rights, property, operations, or safety
              of PACTSOL or another person;
            </li>
            <li>
              to establish, exercise, defend, or resolve a legal or
              commercial claim;
            </li>
            <li>
              in connection with professional legal, accounting, audit,
              insurance, or compliance advice; or
            </li>
            <li>
              as part of a genuine merger, restructuring, transfer,
              investment, sale, or reorganisation of the relevant business,
              subject to applicable legal requirements.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>9. Sale of Personal Information</h2>

          <p>
            PACTSOL's current business model is based on B2B sourcing and
            commercial coordination, not the sale of personal information.
          </p>

          <p>
            PACTSOL does not currently use personal information as a product
            for sale to unrelated third parties for their independent
            marketing databases.
          </p>

          <p>
            This does not prevent PACTSOL from sharing relevant business
            information for legitimate sourcing, supplier coordination,
            professional support, legal compliance, or other purposes
            described in this Policy.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>10. Marketing and Business Communications</h2>

          <p>
            PACTSOL may communicate with existing or prospective business
            contacts regarding sourcing activity, supplier capabilities,
            quotations, enquiries, or other relevant commercial matters
            where such communication is appropriate and lawful.
          </p>

          <p>
            PACTSOL does not intend to send indiscriminate or deceptive
            electronic marketing communications.
          </p>

          <p>
            Where applicable, a recipient may ask PACTSOL to stop sending
            non-essential promotional communications. Such a request does
            not prevent PACTSOL from sending communications reasonably
            necessary to administer an active enquiry, transaction, legal
            obligation, or existing business relationship.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>11. Cookies, Analytics and Technical Data</h2>

          <p>
            The PACTSOL website may use technical features necessary for
            website delivery, security, performance, or basic operation.
          </p>

          <p>
            Hosting providers and internet infrastructure may automatically
            generate limited technical records such as IP address,
            approximate access time, browser or device information,
            requested pages, error information, or security logs.
          </p>

          <p>
            PACTSOL does not currently intend to use behavioural advertising
            technologies as a core part of the website.
          </p>

          <p>
            If PACTSOL later introduces optional analytics, advertising
            technologies, non-essential cookies, or similar tracking
            functionality requiring additional notice or consent, this Policy
            and the website controls should be updated as appropriate.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>12. Information Security</h2>

          <p>
            PACTSOL intends to use reasonable administrative, organisational,
            and technical measures appropriate to the nature of the
            information and the way it is processed.
          </p>

          <p>
            Such measures may include limiting unnecessary access,
            maintaining suitable account security, using reputable service
            providers, maintaining software and infrastructure, and taking
            reasonable steps to reduce unauthorised access, misuse, loss, or
            disclosure.
          </p>

          <p>
            No website, email system, internet transmission, storage system,
            or security measure can be guaranteed to be completely secure.
            PACTSOL therefore cannot promise absolute security or that a
            security incident will never occur.
          </p>

          <p>
            Users should independently protect their own devices, email
            accounts, passwords, networks, and communication systems.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>13. Data Retention</h2>

          <p>
            PACTSOL may retain information for as long as reasonably
            necessary for the purpose for which it was collected or for
            related legitimate business purposes.
          </p>

          <p>
            Relevant considerations may include the duration of a sourcing
            enquiry or business relationship, quotation validity,
            transaction administration, accounting and tax requirements,
            legal or contractual record-keeping obligations, dispute
            management, fraud prevention, and the need to maintain reasonable
            business records.
          </p>

          <p>
            Information may be deleted, anonymised, archived, or otherwise
            restricted when PACTSOL determines that continued active use is
            no longer reasonably necessary, subject to applicable legal,
            contractual, technical, or record-retention requirements.
          </p>

          <p>
            PACTSOL does not promise a single universal retention period for
            every category of information because different business records
            may legitimately require different retention periods.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>14. International Processing and Service Providers</h2>

          <p>
            Some technology, communications, hosting, email, or other service
            providers used by PACTSOL may operate infrastructure in more than
            one country.
          </p>

          <p>
            As a result, information may in some circumstances be stored,
            transmitted, or processed outside the location from which it was
            originally submitted.
          </p>

          <p>
            Where applicable law imposes requirements or restrictions on
            such processing or transfers, PACTSOL will seek to handle the
            relevant processing in accordance with those requirements.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>15. Your Privacy Requests</h2>

          <p>
            Subject to applicable law, the nature of the information, and
            any lawful exceptions, individuals may contact PACTSOL to request
            appropriate assistance concerning personal information relating
            to them.
          </p>

          <p>
            Depending on the law applicable at the relevant time, such a
            request may concern access, correction, updating, completion,
            erasure, withdrawal of consent where consent is the applicable
            basis, or another legally recognised privacy right.
          </p>

          <p>
            PACTSOL may need to verify the identity or authority of the
            person making a request before acting on it. PACTSOL may also
            retain information where continued retention is required or
            permitted by applicable law or reasonably necessary for a legal
            obligation, transaction record, dispute, fraud-prevention
            purpose, or establishment or defence of legal rights.
          </p>

          <p>
            A request should provide sufficient information for PACTSOL to
            understand what information or interaction it relates to.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>16. Withdrawal of Consent</h2>

          <p>
            Where PACTSOL processes particular personal information on the
            basis of consent and applicable law provides a right to withdraw
            that consent, the individual may communicate the withdrawal to
            PACTSOL.
          </p>

          <p>
            Withdrawal will apply prospectively and will not automatically
            invalidate processing that was lawful before the withdrawal.
          </p>

          <p>
            In some circumstances, withdrawing necessary information may
            prevent PACTSOL from continuing a sourcing enquiry or providing
            a particular service.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>17. Business Records and Legal Requirements</h2>

          <p>
            A request to erase or stop using information does not necessarily
            require deletion of every related record in every circumstance.
          </p>

          <p>
            PACTSOL may retain or process information where reasonably
            necessary and permitted by law for accounting, tax, statutory,
            contractual, fraud-prevention, security, dispute-resolution,
            evidence, compliance, or legal-claims purposes.
          </p>

          <p>
            This provision is intended to preserve legitimate record-keeping
            obligations and does not override rights that cannot lawfully be
            restricted.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>18. Information Concerning Children</h2>

          <p>
            PACTSOL is a business-to-business sourcing service and is not
            intended to solicit business enquiries from children.
          </p>

          <p>
            Users submitting sourcing or supplier information should be
            adults authorised to participate in the relevant business
            interaction.
          </p>

          <p>
            If PACTSOL becomes aware that information concerning a child has
            been submitted unnecessarily, PACTSOL may take reasonable steps
            to remove or restrict that information, subject to applicable
            legal requirements.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>19. Third-Party Websites and Services</h2>

          <p>
            The PACTSOL website or communications may contain links,
            references, contact details, or integrations involving
            third-party websites or services.
          </p>

          <p>
            Third parties operate under their own privacy, security, and
            business practices. PACTSOL does not control those independent
            practices merely because a third-party service is referenced,
            linked, or used in connection with a business interaction.
          </p>

          <p>
            Users should review relevant third-party policies where
            appropriate before independently providing information to those
            services.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>20. Confidential Business Information</h2>

          <p>
            This Privacy Policy primarily concerns personal information. It
            does not, by itself, create a general confidentiality obligation
            covering every commercial document, product specification,
            quotation, drawing, trade secret, or other business information
            provided to PACTSOL.
          </p>

          <p>
            Where formal confidentiality protection is required for
            commercially sensitive information, the relevant parties should
            consider an appropriate non-disclosure or confidentiality
            agreement before disclosure.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>21. Accuracy of Information</h2>

          <p>
            Customers, suppliers, and other users are responsible for
            providing information that is accurate and not misleading.
          </p>

          <p>
            Users should inform PACTSOL where material business contact,
            delivery, supplier, or other relevant information previously
            provided has changed and the change may affect an ongoing
            interaction.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>22. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>

          <p>
            PACTSOL may update this Privacy Policy where reasonably necessary
            to reflect changes in its website, sourcing processes, service
            providers, business practices, technology, or applicable legal
            requirements.
          </p>

          <p>
            The current version will be published on the PACTSOL website with
            its last-updated date.
          </p>

          <p>
            Where applicable law requires additional notice or another action
            for a material change, PACTSOL will seek to take the required
            action.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>23. Applicable Privacy Law</h2>

          <p>
            PACTSOL intends to handle personal information in accordance with
            privacy and data-protection requirements applicable to its
            activities in India as those requirements come into force and
            apply to the relevant processing.
          </p>

          <p>
            Indian data-protection law is subject to statutory commencement
            dates, implementing rules, notifications, exemptions,
            interpretations, and regulatory developments. This Policy should
            therefore not be read as a representation that every provision
            of every data-protection law is already operative or applies in
            the same manner to every PACTSOL activity.
          </p>

          <p>
            Nothing in this Policy is intended to exclude or restrict a
            privacy right or obligation that cannot lawfully be excluded.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>24. Contact PACTSOL About Privacy</h2>

          <p>
            Questions, corrections, or privacy-related requests concerning
            information handled by PACTSOL may be directed to:
          </p>

          <address class="legal-page__contact">
            <strong>PACTSOL</strong><br />
            Managed B2B Sourcing<br />
            Email:&nbsp;<a href="mailto:hello@pactsol.in">
              hello@pactsol.in
            </a><br />
            Telephone:&nbsp;<a href="tel:+917989244563">
              +91 7989 244 563
            </a>
          </address>

          <p class="legal-page__contact-note">
            Please identify the relevant enquiry, business interaction, or
            contact information sufficiently for PACTSOL to understand and
            appropriately evaluate the request.
          </p>
        </section>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .legal-page {
      width: 100%;
      padding: 72px 0;
      background: var(--color-warm);
    }

    .legal-page__container {
      max-width: 980px;
    }

    .legal-page__header {
      max-width: 820px;
    }

    .legal-page__eyebrow {
      margin: 0 0 12px;
      color: var(--color-accent);
      font-size: 0.82rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.1em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .legal-page__header h1 {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--color-primary);
      font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
      line-height: 1.1;
      letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    }

    .legal-page__updated {
      margin: 16px 0 0;
      color: var(--color-secondary);
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      font-weight: 600;
    }

    .legal-page__intro {
      margin: 24px 0 0;
      color: var(--color-text);
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      line-height: 1.8;
    }

    .legal-page__notice {
      margin-top: 36px;
      padding: 22px 24px;
      border-left: 4px solid var(--color-secondary);
      border-radius: 6px;
      background: var(--color-white);
      color: var(--color-text);
      font-size: 0.96rem;
      line-height: 1.75;
    }

    .legal-page__notice strong {
      color: var(--color-primary);
    }

    .legal-page__content {
      margin-top: 46px;
    }

    .legal-page__content section {
      padding: 30px 0;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--color-light);
    }

    .legal-page__content h2 {
      margin: 0 0 18px;
      color: var(--color-primary);
      font-size: 1.4rem;
      line-height: 1.35;
    }

    .legal-page__content p {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--color-text);
      font-size: 0.98rem;
      line-height: 1.8;
    }

    .legal-page__content p + p {
      margin-top: 16px;
    }

    .legal-page__content ul {
      margin: 16px 0 0;
      padding-left: 24px;
      color: var(--color-text);
    }

    .legal-page__content li {
      margin: 8px 0;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .legal-page__contact {
      margin-top: 16px;
      color: var(--color-text);
      font-style: normal;
      line-height: 1.8;
    }

    .legal-page__contact strong {
      color: var(--color-primary);
    }

    .legal-page__contact a {
      color: var(--color-primary);
      font-weight: 600;
      text-decoration: none;
    }

    .legal-page__contact a:hover,
    .legal-page__contact a:focus-visible {
      text-decoration: underline;
    }

    .legal-page__contact-note {
      margin-top: 18px !important;
    }

    @media (max-width: 1023px) {
      .legal-page {
        padding: 64px 0;
      }
    }

    @media (max-width: 600px) {
      .legal-page {
        padding: 48px 0;
      }

      .legal-page__header h1 {
        font-size: 2.35rem;
      }

      .legal-page__notice {
        margin-top: 28px;
        padding: 20px;
      }

      .legal-page__content {
        margin-top: 36px;
      }

      .legal-page__content section {
        padding: 26px 0;
      }

      .legal-page__content h2 {
        font-size: 1.25rem;
      }

      .legal-page__content p,
      .legal-page__content li {
        font-size: 0.95rem;
      }
    }
  </style>
</Layout>
